# StarDust UI: config store location (ask before AppData edits)

This file is not a tool or filesystem prohibition. Keep UI state at `%APPDATA%\StarDust` (layout, mode, history, WebView2 profile). Do not put that store in the git repo or change `config_dir()` / `layout_file()` off APPDATA.

- **Read** Windows AppData (Roaming, Local, LocalLow), including `%APPDATA%\StarDust`, is allowed without asking.
- **Edit** (Write, Shell that mutates, copy, delete, rename, move, create) under those trees: **ask first**, every time — path, what will change, and why. Do not edit until Developer answers yes. Do not treat a prior yes as a session-wide pass.
- The StarDust **in-app** agent has its own hidden AppData lock (sidecar / first-turn hint; see `stardust-ui/StarDust UI.md` and `stardust-ui/desktop-drive.md`). That lock is not Cursor’s permission to write without asking.

Example: do not Write `%APPDATA%\StarDust\ui-mode.json` to flip UI mode. Ask: “May I set `ui-mode.json` mode to windows?” Wait for yes.
